<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I10f45bd15df293f63401c295c5dce833543c50da" commit="86fb16a917ca7c50ba654636a39b311d9d8ea550" commit_message="tpm2: refactor tpm2 return value processing  There is no point in checking and reporting error code in each function calling tpm_process_command(), let's do it in one place for all commands.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=Kevin still boots to chrome os  Change-Id: I10f45bd15df293f63401c295c5dce833543c50da Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358174 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Darren Krahn &lt;dkrahn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358174" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/74/358174/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib16bdf782f18a6106eadb4b880cd1e67b56ad6db" commit="57f26d7535742ff845194138eca2b9af9c5e3072" commit_message="vb2api: pad digest buffers if they are larger than digest sizes  Extending tpm PCRs in case of TPM2 requires 32 bit values, some digests pre-calculated in vboot source code are 20 bytes in size. To make sure that PCR extension is consistent, pad remaining buffer space when a 20 byte digest is returned in a 32 byte buffer.  BRANCH=none BUG=chrome-os-partner:50645 TEST=did not verify much, made sure that PCR extension commands      triggered by coreboot succeed.  Change-Id: Ib16bdf782f18a6106eadb4b880cd1e67b56ad6db Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358175 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="358175" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos